h,k) and minimum = the minimum value of y."}},{"kp_id":"law-of-sines-cosines/kp1","kind":"template","arguments":{"statement":"For two existing triangles, lowercase letters denote sides and uppercase letters denote their opposite angles. The first has known measurements {a}; the second has known measurements {b}. Choose the law that starts finding missing measurements in each triangle (use the angle sum first when needed). For side-side-angle data, find an opposite angle first; checking the number of possible triangles is a later step. Answer first = Law of Sines or Law of Cosines; second = Law of Sines or Law of Cosines.","answer_expr":"multipart(trianglelaw(a),trianglelaw(b))","solution_sketch":"For each list ({a} and {b}), count known sides and angles and check whether a known angle is included between known sides. SSS and SAS start with the cosine rule; two angles plus a side supply a sine-rule pair after the angle sum. SSA already has an opposite pair for the sine rule.","hints":["Which measurements form an opposite side-angle pair or an included angle?"],"params":{"a":{"kind":"choice","values":["a,b,c","b,c,A","A,B,a","A,a,b"]},"b":{"kind":"choice","values":["a,b,c","b,c,A","A,B,a","A,a,b"]}},"constraints":[],"samples":[{"params":{"a":"a,b,c","b":"a,b,c"},"expected":"first = Law of Cosines; second = Law of Cosines"},{"params":{"a":"a,b,c","b":"b,c,A"},"expected":"first = Law of Cosines; second = Law of Cosines"},{"params":{"a":"a,b,c","b":"A,B,a"},"expected":"first = Law of Cosines; second = Law of Sines"},{"params":{"a":"a,b,c","b":"A,a,b"},"expected":"first = Law of Cosines; second = Law of Sines"},{"params":{"a":"b,c,A","b":"a,b,c"},"expected":"first = Law of Cosines; second = Law of Cosines"},{"params":{"a":"b,c,A","b":"b,c,A"},"expected":"first = Law of Cosines; second = Law of Cosines"},{"params":{"a":"b,c,A","b":"A,B,a"},"expected":"first = Law of Cosines; second = Law of Sines"},{"params":{"a":"b,c,A","b":"A,a,b"},"expected":"first = Law of Cosines; sec